{"at":"2026-10-30T08:13:25.599Z","type":"item.ingested","item":{"id":"it-fec6b2dd438a","origin":"readwise","originId":"readwise-1001","kind":"highlight","title":"Benchmarks 2026: Mid-Market Churn","capturedAt":"2026-10-21T09:00:00Z","status":"ready","hasMedia":false},"segments":[{"id":"it-fec6b2dd438a-s0","itemId":"it-fec6b2dd438a","seq":0,"text":"Benchmarks 2026: mid-market SaaS logo churn clusters at 6-8% a year across 140 private companies, with a median of 7.1%. Vendors reporting under 2% are usually quoting net revenue churn after expansion, annualizing a single good quarter, or computing logo churn after removing downgrades. Always ask which definition a deck uses, and get the logo number before discussing expansion.","locator":"https://example.com/churn-benchmarks"}],"contentHash":"f0ef755fb07f20bcd801560783be015e73283f34ff87c3b62faea264b243c2bc","api":null}
{"at":"2026-10-30T08:13:25.604Z","type":"claims.extracted","sourceId":"it-fec6b2dd438a","itemId":"it-fec6b2dd438a","claims":[{"id":"cl-fec6b2dd-0","sourceId":"it-fec6b2dd438a","segmentId":"it-fec6b2dd438a-s0","entity":"churn","metric":"churn","value":"see quote","quote":"Benchmarks 2026: mid-market SaaS logo churn clusters at 6-8% a year across 140 private companies, with a median of 7.1%."}],"api":{"model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","responseId":"fake_extract_normal","usage":{"inputTokens":0,"outputTokens":0,"costUsd":0},"stageKey":"ba8b716c083d7600"}}
{"at":"2026-10-30T08:13:25.604Z","type":"item.ingested","item":{"id":"it-8da1dd13fffd","origin":"readwise","originId":"readwise-1002","kind":"highlight","title":"Reading NDR Without Fooling Yourself","capturedAt":"2026-10-22T09:00:00Z","status":"ready","hasMedia":false},"segments":[{"id":"it-8da1dd13fffd-s0","itemId":"it-8da1dd13fffd","seq":0,"text":"Net revenue retention above 115% usually means the vendor expands inside existing accounts faster than it loses them. It says nothing about how many logos leave. Read NDR and logo churn as a pair, never alone.","locator":"https://example.com/reading-ndr"},{"id":"it-8da1dd13fffd-s1","itemId":"it-8da1dd13fffd","seq":1,"text":"Expansion masks churn on a predictable schedule: a base losing 7% of logos a year can print 115-120% NDR for years if the survivors grow seats 20% or more. The tell is gross retention. If gross retention trails the category median of 90%, the bucket is leaking no matter what NDR says.","locator":"https://example.com/reading-ndr"}],"contentHash":"48952464cb4d5b43d4bb86de589008ba651943e911b83a877fc842a64c9ceb04","api":null}
{"at":"2026-10-30T08:13:25.606Z","type":"claims.extracted","sourceId":"it-8da1dd13fffd","itemId":"it-8da1dd13fffd","claims":[{"id":"cl-8da1dd13-0","sourceId":"it-8da1dd13fffd","segmentId":"it-8da1dd13fffd-s0","entity":"churn","metric":"churn","value":"see quote","quote":"Net revenue retention above 115% usually means the vendor expands inside existing accounts faster than it loses them."}],"api":{"model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","responseId":"fake_extract_normal","usage":{"inputTokens":0,"outputTokens":0,"costUsd":0},"stageKey":"0991dcf8581e0d43"}}
{"at":"2026-10-30T08:13:25.607Z","type":"item.ingested","item":{"id":"it-09bac4dce6b3","origin":"readwise","originId":"readwise-1003","kind":"highlight","title":"Second Meetings That Work","capturedAt":"2026-10-23T09:00:00Z","status":"ready","hasMedia":false},"segments":[{"id":"it-09bac4dce6b3-s0","itemId":"it-09bac4dce6b3","seq":0,"text":"Second meetings are for disproving the thesis, not confirming it. Go in with one number to break and one question the founders hope you will not ask.","locator":"https://example.com/second-meetings"},{"id":"it-09bac4dce6b3-s1","itemId":"it-09bac4dce6b3","seq":1,"text":"Open with the benchmark, then let the CFO define the metric before reacting. Write down exact numbers, not adjectives. A founder who answers the definition question precisely usually has nothing to hide; a founder who reframes it is telling you where the bodies are.","locator":"https://example.com/second-meetings"}],"contentHash":"e7960b2ae6bd0da2d41be03f90122c9fffdb87f685bb3581c5ff02efd4fc8428","api":null}
{"at":"2026-10-30T08:13:25.609Z","type":"claims.extracted","sourceId":"it-09bac4dce6b3","itemId":"it-09bac4dce6b3","claims":[{"id":"cl-09bac4dc-0","sourceId":"it-09bac4dce6b3","segmentId":"it-09bac4dce6b3-s0","entity":"general","quote":"Second meetings are for disproving the thesis, not confirming it."}],"api":{"model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","responseId":"fake_extract_normal","usage":{"inputTokens":0,"outputTokens":0,"costUsd":0},"stageKey":"020535aaea7952f1"}}
{"at":"2026-10-30T08:13:25.610Z","type":"item.ingested","item":{"id":"it-252f2c176e84","origin":"vault","originId":"Helios prep.md","kind":"note","title":"Helios prep","capturedAt":"2026-10-30T07:13:24.649Z","status":"ready","hasMedia":false},"segments":[{"id":"it-252f2c176e84-s0","itemId":"it-252f2c176e84","seq":0,"text":"Second meeting, Oct 29. Helios is a mid-market workflow SaaS company raising a $12M Series A. CEO Dana Reyes, CFO Priya Nair. First meeting Oct 21 covered product and go-to-market; this one is about the numbers.","locator":"#Helios prep"},{"id":"it-252f2c176e84-s1","itemId":"it-252f2c176e84","seq":1,"text":"Net churn 1.8%, NDR 118%. No logo churn figure anywhere in the deck. Gross retention mentioned once, without a number. The appendix has a cohort chart but the axes start in 2025, so there is one year of history.","locator":"#What the deck claims"},{"id":"it-252f2c176e84-s2","itemId":"it-252f2c176e84","seq":2,"text":"1. What is logo churn, trailing twelve months, with downgrades counted as churn? This is the number to get first, before any discussion of expansion.\n2. How much of the 118% NDR comes from seat expansion versus price increases? If it is mostly price, the expansion story is thinner than it looks.\n3. What share of the base is on annual versus monthly terms? Monthly-heavy bases churn faster and the sample says so.\n4. Which customer segment churns most, by size and by use case? If the churn concentrates in one segment, the rest of the base may be fine.","locator":"#Open questions"},{"id":"it-252f2c176e84-s3","itemId":"it-252f2c176e84","seq":3,"text":"Open with the benchmark: category logo churn runs 6–8% a year per [[Oct 20 conference notes]], so a 1.8% net figure needs its definition on the table. Let the CFO define it before reacting. Then walk the four questions in order and write down exact numbers, not adjectives.","locator":"#Plan"},{"id":"it-252f2c176e84-s4","itemId":"it-252f2c176e84","seq":4,"text":"[[NDR vs logo churn]] has the math for how 118% NDR and 1.8% net coexist with 7% logo churn. Read it before the meeting.","locator":"#Background"}],"contentHash":"d1377e4a4a4da94ebff45d31907c9db68c63202b3181df294b4ef371e0593809","api":null}
{"at":"2026-10-30T08:13:25.613Z","type":"claims.extracted","sourceId":"it-252f2c176e84","itemId":"it-252f2c176e84","claims":[{"id":"cl-252f2c17-0","sourceId":"it-252f2c176e84","segmentId":"it-252f2c176e84-s0","entity":"churn","metric":"churn","value":"see quote","quote":"Second meeting, Oct 29."}],"api":{"model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","responseId":"fake_extract_normal","usage":{"inputTokens":0,"outputTokens":0,"costUsd":0},"stageKey":"6f287c2a03f641b7"}}
{"at":"2026-10-30T08:13:25.614Z","type":"item.ingested","item":{"id":"it-273751ede708","origin":"vault","originId":"NDR vs logo churn.md","kind":"note","title":"NDR vs logo churn","capturedAt":"2026-10-30T07:13:24.649Z","status":"ready","hasMedia":false},"segments":[{"id":"it-273751ede708-s0","itemId":"it-273751ede708","seq":0,"text":"Reading note. NDR and logo churn answer different questions and decks love quoting the flattering one.","locator":"#NDR vs logo churn"},{"id":"it-273751ede708-s1","itemId":"it-273751ede708","seq":1,"text":"Take 100 customers paying $1 each. Seven leave (7% logo churn), the survivors expand to $1.25 on average. Ending revenue is $116 on a $100 base: 116% NDR, while nearly one in ten logos walked out. Add one noisy quarter of price increases and you get 118% NDR next to 1.8% net churn with the same 7% logo churn underneath. All three numbers can be true at once.","locator":"#The math"},{"id":"it-273751ede708-s2","itemId":"it-273751ede708","seq":2,"text":"The deck's 1.8% net churn and 118% NDR tell us expansion is working. They say nothing about how many logos leave, which is what determines whether the go-to-market engine has to refill the bucket every year. A company can grow 2x into its Series A on expansion and still have a leaky base.","locator":"#Why it matters for Helios"},{"id":"it-273751ede708-s3","itemId":"it-273751ede708","seq":3,"text":"- Gross retention, trailing twelve months, no adjustments.\n- Logo churn split by cohort year: is it improving as the product matures?\n- Expansion concentrated in a few accounts, or broad-based?","locator":"#Questions this raises"},{"id":"it-273751ede708-s4","itemId":"it-273751ede708","seq":4,"text":"Filed under [[Helios prep]].","locator":"#Questions this raises"}],"contentHash":"a0f205106a5987a7199aa19e64f7eeaed6bc036768a766e3bceb066ff41d4f03","api":null}
{"at":"2026-10-30T08:13:25.617Z","type":"claims.extracted","sourceId":"it-273751ede708","itemId":"it-273751ede708","claims":[{"id":"cl-273751ed-0","sourceId":"it-273751ede708","segmentId":"it-273751ede708-s0","entity":"churn","metric":"churn","value":"see quote","quote":"Reading note."}],"api":{"model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","responseId":"fake_extract_normal","usage":{"inputTokens":0,"outputTokens":0,"costUsd":0},"stageKey":"8dbaef62898f110c"}}
{"at":"2026-10-30T08:13:25.617Z","type":"item.ingested","item":{"id":"it-f650168cfa2b","origin":"vault","originId":"oct-20-conference.md","kind":"note","title":"Oct 20 conference notes","capturedAt":"2026-10-30T07:13:24.649Z","status":"ready","hasMedia":false},"segments":[{"id":"it-f650168cfa2b-s0","itemId":"it-f650168cfa2b","seq":0,"text":"Notes on the mid-market SaaS churn benchmarks talk, Oct 20. 90 seconds of Q&A at the end mattered more than the slides.","locator":"#Oct 20 conference notes"},{"id":"it-f650168cfa2b-s1","itemId":"it-f650168cfa2b","seq":1,"text":"140 private SaaS companies, $5–50M ARR, FY2025 numbers, self-reported with investor verification on about half. Mid-market defined as 200–2000 employees at the customer. The speaker works at the benchmarking firm full time; this is their flagship dataset, not a vendor survey.","locator":"#The sample"},{"id":"it-f650168cfa2b-s2","itemId":"it-f650168cfa2b","seq":2,"text":"- Logo churn clusters at 6–8% a year. Median 7.1%. Nobody in the sample holds under 5% without annual prepays plus an embedded workflow.\n- Net revenue churn medians 3.1% after expansion. The gap between logo and net is the whole story: expansion dollars hide departing logos.\n- Top quartile keeps gross retention above 90% by selling multi-year terms into operations teams, where switching costs are highest.","locator":"#The numbers"},{"id":"it-f650168cfa2b-s3","itemId":"it-f650168cfa2b","seq":3,"text":"Anyone quoting under two percent is measuring something else. Usually one of three things: net revenue churn quoted without the word net, a single trailing quarter annualized, or logo churn computed after removing downgrades and contractions. Ask which one before believing it.","locator":"#The 2% rule"},{"id":"it-f650168cfa2b-s4","itemId":"it-f650168cfa2b","seq":4,"text":"One audience question, worth writing down: does the 6–8% include downgrades, or logo churn only? Answer: logo churn only. Net revenue churn with expansion is a different story, and decks that blend the two in one chart should be read with suspicion.","locator":"#Q&A"},{"id":"it-f650168cfa2b-s5","itemId":"it-f650168cfa2b","seq":5,"text":"[[Helios prep]]: the deck says net churn 1.8%. Against this sample that number can only be net of expansion, and aggressive expansion at that. Go in asking for the logo number and the definition. See also [[NDR vs logo churn]] for the math.","locator":"#Takeaway"}],"contentHash":"b43666e45ec780b7ec1ace9cabdc88ecb3598cc0c75b0ae9e323761ea415b5f2","api":null}
